    <textTemplates>
        <name>terminationBody</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>Dear {!Get_Opp_Id.Name},

I hope this message finds you well.

This letter serves as a formal Termination Notice concerning the non-payment of the stamp duty amount due for the registration process, despite having received three prior reminders from our office. As of today, the required stamp duty amount of {!Get_Opp_Id.EYI_SD_Balance_Amount__c} remains unpaid, and we have not received any response from your side.

As stated in our previous communications, payment of the stamp duty was necessary for the progression of your booking. Unfortunately, due to the continued non-payment and lack of response, we hereby inform you that your booking for {!Get_Opp_Id.EYI_Inventory__r.Name} is being terminated, effective as of {!today}. Consequently, the unit will be released and made available for other interested parties.

Please be aware that, as per the terms of the agreement, failure to pay the stamp duty will result in the forfeiture of any advance payments made and the cancellation of all associated services. Should the payment not be received by the effective termination date, we will consider the matter concluded, and no further action will be taken.

While we regret the necessity of this decision, we are providing a final opportunity for you to settle the payment before the termination becomes final. Kindly remit the outstanding stamp duty by [insert final payment date]. After this date, no further arrangements will be made, and the booking will be permanently canceled.

We sincerely hope to resolve this matter promptly. If you have any questions or require assistance, please do not hesitate to contact us.

Thank you for your attention to this matter.

Best regards,
{!Get_Opp_Id.EYI_Relationship_Manager__r.Name}
Relationship Manager
Panchshil Realty
{!Get_Opp_Id.EYI_Relationship_Manager__r.MobilePhone}</text>
